{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt4\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> The relationship between two <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/entity\" title=\"entity\">entities</a> in which one <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/entity\" title=\"entity\">entity</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/inherit\" title=\"inherit\">inherits</a> from the other."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt7\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Such a relationship expressed as an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ontology%20components\" title=\"w:ontology components\" about=\"#mwt8\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" class=\"extiw\">ontology component</a> (regardless of whether the OOP paradigm per se is implemented)."}]}]}